# magic-worlds SPA — Vite env. Copy to .env and adjust for your machine.
# Only VITE_-prefixed vars are exposed to the browser (see src/infrastructure/api/baseUrl.ts).

# REQUIRED — base URL of the magic-worlds-api BFF (NOT api.auth directly).
# Every credentialed auth call sends credentials:'include' for the BFF's
# HttpOnly mw_refresh_token cookie. Configure it to match deployment:
# Local/LAN same-site HTTP uses SameSite=lax and Secure=false. `{hostname}` is
# replaced with the page's hostname at runtime, so one value works everywhere:
#   page http://localhost:5173    -> API http://localhost:8010
#   page http://192.168.1.13:5173 -> API http://192.168.1.13:8010
# Cross-site production uses the BFF's absolute HTTPS URL, SameSite=None,
# Secure=true, and the exact SPA origin in credentialed CORS allow-lists.
# SameSite=None cookies may still be blocked by third-party-cookie policy.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://{hostname}:8010

# Temporary product access is supplied by GET /user/me/features and each user's
# membership plan. There are no frontend feature environment variables.
# Missing/null grants are off; root bypasses rollout restrictions. Workspaces
# is globally released and has no feature permission.

# --- Google sign-in ("Continue with Google") ---------------------------------
# NO extra SPA variable is required. The flow uses VITE_API_BASE_URL (it calls the
# BFF's /auth/provider-init/google, /auth/google/start/shim, /auth/google/exchange)
# and window.location.origin as the return origin. To enable it end to end, the
# SPA's actual origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) MUST be listed in:
#   - the BFF's   PROVIDER_INIT_RETURN_ORIGINS  (and CORS_ORIGINS)
#   - api.auth's  GOOGLE_OAUTH_RETURN_ORIGINS
# and the BFF's FRONTEND_GOOGLE_RETURN_URL must point back at this origin.

# Billing availability comes from GET /billing/plans. Configure billing,
# Patreon, assistants and providers on the BFF; the browser has no kill switches.
# Text generation uses the streaming transport supplied by the current BFF.
